WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.010
The clipped posterior dominates both maximum
likelihood and the un clipped Bayesian posterior.

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.100
It guarantees one hundred percent accuracy on
states where the expert knows the single best action,

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:12.190
in every data and optimality setting,

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:16.280
whereas maximum likelihood ranges from sixty seven
to ninety two percent.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.370
It also never selects an action outside the
expert's epsilon ball,

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.460
so it makes no truly bad mistakes.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.550
Strikingly,

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.640
even though the constraints say nothing explicit
about which action to pick in uncertain states,

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.730
our method is still more accurate there than the
baselines,

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:40.820
which means the constraints implicitly transfer the
expert's uncertainty structure.
